# 36. Most Important Constraint

The benchmark suite must not merely produce data that makes Quentra pass.

Expected values must be calculated independently from first principles.

Do not derive:

```text
expected result
```

from:

```text
Quentra result
```

That would make the test meaningless.

The direction must always be:

```text
Engineering definition
        ↓
Independent hand/math calculation
        ↓
Expected result
        ↓
Quentra result
        ↓
Comparison
```

---

# 37. Final Objective

The finished suite should allow a developer on macOS to run:

```bash
dotnet test
```

and get strong confidence that Quentra's quantity engine behaves correctly even though ETABS itself is not installed.

Later, real ETABS snapshots should be added as an additional integration layer rather than replacing the synthetic golden benchmarks.

The final testing architecture should be:

```text
                  QUENTRA TESTING

           ┌──────────────────────┐
           │  Engineering Truth   │
           └──────────┬───────────┘
                      │
              Golden Benchmarks
                      │
        ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
        │                           │
        ▼                           ▼
Synthetic Snapshot          Captured ETABS Snapshot
        │                           │
        └─────────────┬─────────────┘
                      ▼
             Normalized Model
                      ▼
             Quentra Engine
                      ▼
              Actual Result
                      ▼
           Expected Comparison
                      ▼
                 PASS / FAIL
```

The purpose is not to pretend synthetic data is ETABS.

The purpose is to make Quentra's calculation engine testable, reproducible, and independently verifiable now, while making the same suite ready to accept genuine ETABS API captures later.
